\ Deadline: the grounds as pictures. Every outdoor picture shows the same
\ house, placed in metres: its south front along z 0 from x -10 to 10, its
\ back along z 12, two storeys to the eaves at 7 m and the roof ridge at 10 m
\ running east and west. The front door is at x 0, the bay window of the
\ living room west of it, the small locked window east of it; at the back
\ are the dining room's picture window and the library balcony to the west,
\ the kitchen window and the bedroom balcony to the east. The lake lies
\ beyond the north lawn and along the west and east shores; the shed stands
\ on the east lawn beside the water. The sun is the lamp, low in the
\ south-east of the morning.

\ how fast lines fade with distance out of doors, and indoors after
0.035 constant outdoor-fading
0.12 constant indoor-fading

\ set the global distance fade
: outdoor-fade! ( rate -- )
	| rate ^fade |
	rate to fade ;

\ begin an outdoor picture: the camera where it stands, the sun as the lamp, lines fading slowly
: outdoor-view ( x y z yaw pitch focal -- )
	| x y z yaw pitch focal |
	x y z yaw pitch focal new-picture
	[ 60 45 -50 ] lamp!
	outdoor-fading outdoor-fade! ;

\ the end of an outdoor picture: lines fade as indoors again for what is drawn next
: outdoor-done ( -- ) indoor-fading outdoor-fade! ;

\ === surfaces seen from outside ===

\ the centre of a polygon's corners
: corner-centre ( points -- point )
	| points |
	points [ 0 0 0 ] ( total corner | total corner ' + 2 nmap ) reduce
	( points size / ) map ;

\ fill a polygon with a light, the part of it behind the camera cut away, so a wall beside the camera still hides what is behind it
: near-fill ( points light -- )
	| points light |
	points ( point | [ point to-camera ] ) map to corners
	[ ] to kept
	0 corners size 1 do k
		corners k @i to a
		corners k 1 + corners size mod @i to b
		a 2 @i nearest-depth >= to a-ahead
		b 2 @i nearest-depth >= to b-ahead
		a-ahead if kept a add-last! drop then
		a-ahead b-ahead = not if
			nearest-depth a 2 @i - b 2 @i a 2 @i - / to cut
			kept [ 0 3 1 do axis a axis @i b axis @i a axis @i - cut * + loop ] add-last! drop
		then
	loop
	kept size 3 < if exit then
	[ ] to xs
	[ ] to ys
	kept ( corner | corner spread to-screen to sy to sx xs sx add-last! drop ys sy add-last! drop ) each
	xs ys light kept polygon-plane fill-screen-polygon ;

\ whether a flat face of a solid, its corners and outward normal, is turned toward the camera
: face-seen? ( points normal -- flag )
	| points normal |
	points corner-centre normal facing-camera? ;

\ outline a face turned toward the camera, as bright as the sun lights it
: sunlit-face ( points normal brightness -- )
	| points normal brightness |
	points normal face-seen? not if exit then
	points corner-centre normal brightness lamp-light pen!
	points outline ;

\ a window in a wall facing north or south, at z, its frame, cross bars and sill; its glass dark, or lit from a lamp within for some windows
: facade-window ( west east bottom top z outward brightness -- )
	| west east bottom top z outward brightness |
	z outward 0.03 * + to front
	[ [ west bottom front ] [ east bottom front ] [ east top front ] [ west top front ] ] to frame
	west 3.1 * top 1.7 * + z 0.37 * + hash-fraction 0.62 > to lit-within
	frame lit-within if 0.3 else 0.035 then near-fill
	lit-within if frame corner-centre east west - 0.9 * 0.18 glow then
	frame corner-centre [ 0 0 outward ] brightness lamp-light to light
	light pen!
	frame outline
	light 0.55 * pen!
	west east + 2 / to middle
	middle bottom front middle top front edge
	west top bottom - 0.45 * bottom + front east top bottom - 0.45 * bottom + front edge
	light 1.2 * pen!
	west 0.08 - bottom 0.04 - z outward 0.08 * + east 0.08 + bottom 0.04 - z outward 0.08 * + edge ;

\ === the ground, the lake and the sky ===

\ faint strokes of grass scattered over a stretch of lawn
: grass-strokes ( west east south north count seed -- )
	| west east south north count seed |
	0 count 1 do k
		seed k 7.13 * + hash-fraction to across
		seed k 3.71 * + 1.3 + hash-fraction to along
		seed k 5.3 * + 2.1 + hash-fraction to tall
		east west - across * west + to x
		north south - along * south + to z
		x 0 z x tall 0.06 * 0.02 - + tall 0.12 * 0.06 + z edge
	loop ;

\ the lawn as faint rows running across the view, closing up with distance, each broken into lengths
: lawn-rows ( west east south north count seed -- )
	| west east south north count seed |
	0 count 1 do k
		north south - k count / * south + to z
		0 6 1 do piece
			seed k 11 * + piece + hash-fraction to chance
			chance 0.35 > if
				east west - piece 6 / * west + to from
				east west - piece chance 0.5 * + 6 / * west + to onto
				from 0 z onto 0 z edge
			then
		loop
	loop ;

\ water from a shore line out to a far edge: dim ripples, brighter glints where the sun catches it
: lake-ripples ( west east south north count seed -- )
	| west east south north count seed |
	0 count 1 do k
		seed k 4.7 * + hash-fraction to across
		seed k 2.3 * + 0.7 + hash-fraction to along
		seed k 6.1 * + 3.3 + hash-fraction to span
		east west - across * west + to x
		north south - along * south + to z
		span 1.5 * 0.3 + to half-length
		span 0.9 > if 0.75 else 0.22 then pen!
		x half-length - -0.05 z x half-length + -0.05 z edge
	loop ;

\ a far shore line across the horizon, low and faint
: far-shore ( west east z height seed -- )
	| west east z height seed |
	0.1 pen!
	[ 0 13 1 do k
		k 12 / to t
		[ east west - t * west + seed k + hash-fraction height * z ]
	loop ] path ;

\ === things on the grounds ===

\ the camera's rightward direction, for shapes drawn facing it
: facing-across ( -- direction ) [ view@cos-yaw 0 view@sin-yaw negate ] ;

\ the leafy crown of a tree or bush: an outline of lumps facing the camera, filled black, with a few leaves inside
: crown-blob ( centre radius seed brightness -- )
	| centre radius seed brightness |
	facing-across to across
	[ 0 1 0 ] to upward
	[ 0 18 1 do k
		k 18 / TAU * to angle
		seed k + hash-fraction 0.3 * 0.85 + radius * to reach
		[ 0 3 1 do axis
			centre axis @i across axis @i angle cos reach * * + upward axis @i angle sin reach * 0.8 * * +
		loop ]
	loop ] to lumps
	lumps 0 near-fill
	lumps corner-centre [ 0 1 0 ] brightness lamp-light pen!
	lumps outline
	brightness 0.35 * pen!
	0 7 1 do k
		seed k 1.7 * + hash-fraction 1.6 * 0.8 - radius * to offset-across
		seed k 2.9 * + hash-fraction 1.2 * 0.6 - radius * to offset-up
		[ 0 3 1 do axis centre axis @i across axis @i offset-across * + upward axis @i offset-up * + loop ] to leaf
		leaf [ 0 3 1 do axis leaf axis @i across axis @i radius 0.18 * * + loop ] segment
	loop ;

\ a fruit tree: a trunk forking into branches under a leafy crown
: fruit-tree ( x z height seed -- )
	| x z height seed |
	height 0.38 * to fork
	0.35 pen!
	x 0.08 - 0 z x 0.05 - fork z edge
	x 0.08 + 0 z x 0.05 + fork z edge
	0 4 1 do k
		seed k + hash-fraction 1.6 * 0.8 - height 0.3 * * to spread-across
		x fork z x spread-across + height 0.7 * z edge
	loop
	[ x height 0.68 * z ] height 0.36 * seed 0.5 crown-blob ;

\ a rose bush: a low round crown dotted with bright blooms
: rose-bush ( x z seed -- )
	| x z seed |
	[ x 0.4 z ] 0.42 seed 0.35 crown-blob
	facing-across to across
	0 4 1 do k
		seed k 3.1 * + hash-fraction 1.4 * 0.7 - 0.3 * to offset-across
		seed k 1.9 * + hash-fraction 0.35 * 0.3 + to bloom-height
		[ x across 0 @i offset-across * + bloom-height z across 2 @i offset-across * + ] to bloom
		0.95 pen!
		bloom 0.02 detail-scale * 0.28 glow
		bloom [ bloom first 0.03 + bloom second bloom 2 @i ] segment
	loop ;

\ a ladder leaning from its foot to its top, rails and rungs, bright enough to catch the eye
: leaning-ladder ( foot top -- )
	| foot top |
	facing-across to across
	[ 0 3 1 do axis across axis @i 0.22 * loop ] to half-width
	foot half-width vector- to left-foot
	foot half-width ' + 2 nmap to right-foot
	top half-width vector- to left-top
	top half-width ' + 2 nmap to right-top
	0.8 pen!
	left-foot left-top segment
	right-foot right-top segment
	0.55 pen!
	1 16 1 do k
		k 16 / to t
		left-foot left-top t between right-foot right-top t between segment
	loop ;

\ a ladder lying flat on the ground from one end to the other
: lying-ladder ( a b -- )
	| a b |
	b a vector- to along
	[ along 2 @i 0 along 0 @i negate ] unit-vector ( 0.22 * ) map to half-width
	a half-width vector- b half-width vector- 0.7 pen! segment
	a half-width ' + 2 nmap b half-width ' + 2 nmap segment
	0.45 pen!
	1 16 1 do k
		k 16 / to t
		a half-width vector- b half-width vector- t between
		a half-width ' + 2 nmap b half-width ' + 2 nmap t between segment
	loop ;

\ a balcony against the back of the house: its floor out from the wall and the railing round it
: balcony-shelf ( west east height depth -- )
	| west east height depth |
	[ [ west height 12 ] [ east height 12 ] [ east height 12 depth + ] [ west height 12 depth + ] ] to deck
	deck 0 near-fill
	0.55 pen!
	deck outline
	west height 0.25 - 12 east height 0.25 - 12 edge
	height 1 + to rail
	0.75 pen!
	[ [ west rail 12 ] [ west rail 12 depth + ] [ east rail 12 depth + ] [ east rail 12 ] ] path
	0.35 pen!
	west east - abs 0.3 / round to n-balusters
	0 n-balusters 1 + 1 do k
		k n-balusters / to t
		west east west - t * + height 12 depth + west east west - t * + rail 12 depth + edge
	loop
	west height 12 depth + west rail 12 depth + edge
	east height 12 depth + east rail 12 depth + edge ;

\ === the house ===

\ the living room's bay window standing out from the front between two xs, its three faces of glass
: bay-window-bulge ( west east -- )
	| west east |
	[ [ west 0 0 ] [ west 0.5 + 0 -1.1 ] [ east 0.5 - 0 -1.1 ] [ east 0 0 ] ] to base
	base ( corner | corner spread to z drop to x [ x 2.9 z ] ) map to crown
	[ base first base second crown second crown first ] to left-face
	[ base second base 2 @i crown 2 @i crown second ] to front-face
	[ base 2 @i base 3 @i crown 3 @i crown 2 @i ] to right-face
	[ left-face front-face right-face ] ( face | face 0 near-fill ) each
	[ [ crown first crown second crown 2 @i crown 3 @i [ east 3.3 0 ] [ west 3.3 0 ] ] ] ( roof | roof 0 near-fill 0.6 pen! roof outline ) each
	0.7 pen!
	base path
	crown path
	[ left-face front-face right-face ] ( face |
		face first face second 0.12 between to low-a
		face first face second 0.88 between to low-b
		[ low-a first 0.5 low-a 2 @i ] to glass-a
		[ low-b first 0.5 low-b 2 @i ] to glass-b
		[ glass-a [ glass-b first 0.5 glass-b 2 @i ] [ glass-b first 2.6 glass-b 2 @i ] [ glass-a first 2.6 glass-a 2 @i ] ] to glass
		glass 0.06 near-fill
		0.65 pen!
		glass outline
		:bay-window :open flag? face front-face = and if
			glass-b first glass-a first - abs 0.5 * to sash
			[ glass-a first sash 0.5 * + 0.5 glass-a 2 @i sash 0.85 * - ] to swung
			[ glass-a swung [ swung first 2.6 swung 2 @i ] [ glass-a first 2.6 glass-a 2 @i ] ] to open-sash
			glass 0 near-fill
			[ glass-a first sash + 1.4 glass-a 2 @i 0.3 + ] 1.1 0.18 glow
			open-sash 0.1 near-fill
			0.85 pen!
			open-sash outline
		then
		0.35 pen!
		glass-a glass-b 0.5 between to foot
		foot [ foot first 2.6 foot 2 @i ] segment
	) each
	0.6 pen!
	base first crown first segment
	base 3 @i crown 3 @i segment
	base second crown second segment
	base 2 @i crown 2 @i segment ;

\ the house, a solid seen from outside: walls and roof filled black, the faces turned toward the camera outlined as the sun lights them, their doors and windows drawn
: robner-house ( -- )
	[ [ -10 0 0 ] [ 10 0 0 ] [ 10 7 0 ] [ -10 7 0 ] ] to south-wall
	[ [ 10 0 12 ] [ -10 0 12 ] [ -10 7 12 ] [ 10 7 12 ] ] to north-wall
	[ [ 10 0 0 ] [ 10 0 12 ] [ 10 7 12 ] [ 10 10 6 ] [ 10 7 0 ] ] to east-wall
	[ [ -10 0 12 ] [ -10 0 0 ] [ -10 7 0 ] [ -10 10 6 ] [ -10 7 12 ] ] to west-wall
	[ [ -10.4 6.8 -0.4 ] [ 10.4 6.8 -0.4 ] [ 10.4 10 6 ] [ -10.4 10 6 ] ] to south-roof
	[ [ 10.4 6.8 12.4 ] [ -10.4 6.8 12.4 ] [ -10.4 10 6 ] [ 10.4 10 6 ] ] to north-roof
	[ south-wall north-wall east-wall west-wall south-roof north-roof ] ( face | face 0 near-fill ) each
	south-wall [ 0 0 -1 ] 0.75 sunlit-face
	north-wall [ 0 0 1 ] 0.75 sunlit-face
	east-wall [ 1 0 0 ] 0.75 sunlit-face
	west-wall [ -1 0 0 ] 0.75 sunlit-face
	south-roof [ 0 0.894 -0.447 ] 0.7 sunlit-face
	north-roof [ 0 0.894 0.447 ] 0.7 sunlit-face
	south-roof [ 0 0.894 -0.447 ] face-seen? if
		0.07 pen!
		[ -10.4 6.8 -0.4 ] [ 10.4 6.8 -0.4 ] [ 10.4 10 6 ] [ -10.4 10 6 ] 14 hatch
	then
	6 9 4.6 7 11.4 5.6 solid-box
	south-wall [ 0 0 -1 ] face-seen? if
		[ -7.5 -4.4 -1.4 1.6 4.4 7.4 ] ( centre | centre 0.55 - centre 0.55 + 4.0 5.6 0 -1 0.7 facade-window ) each
		3.3 4.3 1.1 2.1 0 -1 0.6 facade-window
		[ [ -0.7 0 -0.02 ] [ 0.7 0 -0.02 ] [ 0.7 2.4 -0.02 ] [ -0.7 2.4 -0.02 ] ] to doorway
		:front-door :open flag? if
			doorway 0 near-fill
			0.2 pen!
			doorway outline
			0.55 pen!
			[ [ 0.7 0 -0.02 ] [ 0.7 0 1.3 ] [ 0.7 2.4 1.3 ] [ 0.7 2.4 -0.02 ] ] outline
			[ 0 1.2 3 ] 1.2 0.08 glow
		else
			doorway 0.02 near-fill
			0.75 pen!
			doorway outline
			0.4 pen!
			[ [ -0.55 0.2 -0.03 ] [ -0.05 0.2 -0.03 ] [ -0.05 1.1 -0.03 ] [ -0.55 1.1 -0.03 ] ] outline
			[ [ 0.05 0.2 -0.03 ] [ 0.55 0.2 -0.03 ] [ 0.55 1.1 -0.03 ] [ 0.05 1.1 -0.03 ] ] outline
			[ [ -0.55 1.3 -0.03 ] [ -0.05 1.3 -0.03 ] [ -0.05 2.2 -0.03 ] [ -0.55 2.2 -0.03 ] ] outline
			[ [ 0.05 1.3 -0.03 ] [ 0.55 1.3 -0.03 ] [ 0.55 2.2 -0.03 ] [ 0.05 2.2 -0.03 ] ] outline
			0.9 pen!
			0.45 1.15 -0.06 0.5 1.15 -0.06 edge
		then
		0.5 pen!
		-1.1 0 -0.6 1.1 0.18 0 solid-box
		[ 0.95 2.1 -0.3 ] 0.25 0.35 glow
		-6.5 -2.5 bay-window-bulge
	then
	north-wall [ 0 0 1 ] face-seen? if
		-8 -4.5 0.9 2.4 12 1 0.65 facade-window
		3.5 5.5 1 2.2 12 1 0.6 facade-window
		[ 1 7.5 ] ( centre | centre 0.55 - centre 0.55 + 4.0 5.6 12 1 0.6 facade-window ) each
		-6 -4.5 3.6 6 12 1 0.7 facade-window
		4 5.3 3.6 6 12 1 0.7 facade-window
		-7 -3.5 3.6 1.3 balcony-shelf
		3 6.5 3.6 1.2 balcony-shelf
	then ;

\ === South Lawn ===

\ the house's south front seen from the lawn
: south-lawn-picture ( -- )
	0 1.65 -24 0 0.04 300 outdoor-view
	[ [ [ -2.2 0 -17 ] PI 0.1 + ] [ [ 2.6 0 -16 ] PI 0.15 - ] [ [ -5 0 -13 ] PI 0.3 + ] [ [ 5.5 0 -12 ] PI 0.35 - ] ] spots!
	-60 60 40 4 1 far-shore
	-60 -12 14 40 90 11 lake-ripples
	12 60 14 40 90 23 lake-ripples
	0.06 pen!
	-40 40 -24 14 24 3 lawn-rows
	robner-house
	-16 8 5.5 3 fruit-tree
	15 9 6 7 fruit-tree
	0.35 pen!
	-0.9 0 -24 -0.9 0 -0.6 edge
	0.9 0 -24 0.9 0 -0.6 edge
	0.55 pen!
	0 160 1 do k
		k 0.37 * hash-fraction 1.6 * 0.8 - to across
		k 0.61 * hash-fraction 23 * -23.5 + to along
		across 0.005 along across 0.03 + 0.005 along 0.02 + edge
	loop
	0.14 pen!
	-14 14 -24 -1 160 41 grass-strokes
	outdoor-done ;

\ === more things on the grounds ===

\ a tall picket fence from one point to another along the ground
: garden-fence ( x0 z0 x1 z1 height -- )
	| x0 z0 x1 z1 height |
	[ x0 0 z0 ] [ x1 0 z1 ] vector- dup dot sqrt to span
	span 0.32 / round 1 max2 to n-pickets
	0.4 pen!
	x0 height 0.8 * z0 x1 height 0.8 * z1 edge
	x0 height 0.25 * z0 x1 height 0.25 * z1 edge
	0.2 pen!
	0 n-pickets 1 + 1 do k
		k n-pickets / to t
		x1 x0 - t * x0 + to x
		z1 z0 - t * z0 + to z
		x 0 z x height z edge
	loop ;

\ a grape arbor: posts carrying a lattice of beams, vines hanging from it
: grape-arbor ( west east south north height -- )
	| west east south north height |
	0.4 pen!
	[ [ west south ] [ east south ] [ west north ] [ east north ] ]
	( corner | corner spread to z to x x 0 z x height z edge ) each
	[ [ west height south ] [ east height south ] [ east height north ] [ west height north ] ] 0 near-fill
	0.5 pen!
	[ [ west height south ] [ east height south ] [ east height north ] [ west height north ] ] outline
	0.3 pen!
	[ west height south ] [ east height south ] [ east height north ] [ west height north ] 8 3 grid
	0 12 1 do k
		k 17.7 * hash-fraction east west - * west + to x
		k 9.3 * hash-fraction 0.8 * 0.3 + to hang
		0.25 pen!
		x height south x 0.1 - height hang - south edge
		[ x 0.1 - height hang - south ] 0.05 detail-scale * 0.15 glow
	loop ;

\ the newspaper leaning against the front door, folded, its headline catching the light
: newspaper-at-door ( -- )
	0.2 0.02 -0.18 0.62 0.4 -0.14 solid-box
	0.9 pen!
	[ [ 0.24 0.3 -0.19 ] [ 0.58 0.3 -0.19 ] ] path
	0.5 pen!
	0 4 1 do k
		k 0.06 * 0.08 + to y
		0.24 y -0.19 0.58 y -0.19 edge
	loop ;

\ the shed beside the lake: plank walls, a pitched roof, its door toward the lawn and the one dirty window
: garden-shed ( -- )
	[ [ 25 0 -3.6 ] [ 28 0 -3.6 ] [ 28 2.3 -3.6 ] [ 26.5 3.1 -3.6 ] [ 25 2.3 -3.6 ] ] to north-face
	[ [ 28 0 -6 ] [ 25 0 -6 ] [ 25 2.3 -6 ] [ 26.5 3.1 -6 ] [ 28 2.3 -6 ] ] to south-face
	[ [ 25 0 -6 ] [ 25 0 -3.6 ] [ 25 2.3 -3.6 ] [ 25 2.3 -6 ] ] to west-face
	[ [ 28 0 -3.6 ] [ 28 0 -6 ] [ 28 2.3 -6 ] [ 28 2.3 -3.6 ] ] to east-face
	[ [ 24.8 2.2 -3.4 ] [ 26.5 3.1 -3.4 ] [ 26.5 3.1 -6.2 ] [ 24.8 2.2 -6.2 ] ] to west-roof
	[ [ 28.2 2.2 -6.2 ] [ 26.5 3.1 -6.2 ] [ 26.5 3.1 -3.4 ] [ 28.2 2.2 -3.4 ] ] to east-roof
	[ north-face south-face west-face east-face west-roof east-roof ] ( face | face 0 near-fill ) each
	north-face [ 0 0 1 ] 0.6 sunlit-face
	south-face [ 0 0 -1 ] 0.6 sunlit-face
	west-face [ -1 0 0 ] 0.6 sunlit-face
	east-face [ 1 0 0 ] 0.6 sunlit-face
	west-roof [ -0.47 0.88 0 ] 0.65 sunlit-face
	east-roof [ 0.47 0.88 0 ] 0.65 sunlit-face
	west-face [ -1 0 0 ] face-seen? if
		0.12 pen!
		[ 25 0 -6 ] [ 25 0 -3.6 ] [ 25 2.3 -3.6 ] [ 25 2.3 -6 ] 9 hatch
		[ [ 24.97 1.0 -5.3 ] [ 24.97 1.0 -4.3 ] [ 24.97 1.8 -4.3 ] [ 24.97 1.8 -5.3 ] ] to grimy
		grimy 0.1 near-fill
		0.7 pen!
		grimy outline
		0.18 pen!
		[ 24.96 1.0 -5.3 ] [ 24.96 1.0 -4.3 ] [ 24.96 1.8 -4.3 ] [ 24.96 1.8 -5.3 ] 7 hatch
	then
	north-face [ 0 0 1 ] face-seen? if
		0.12 pen!
		[ 25 0 -3.6 ] [ 25 2.3 -3.6 ] [ 28 2.3 -3.6 ] [ 28 0 -3.6 ] 11 hatch
		[ [ 25.6 0 -3.57 ] [ 26.5 0 -3.57 ] [ 26.5 1.95 -3.57 ] [ 25.6 1.95 -3.57 ] ] to door
		door 0.02 near-fill
		0.65 pen!
		door outline
		0.9 pen!
		26.35 1.0 -3.54 26.4 1.0 -3.54 edge
	then
	south-face [ 0 0 -1 ] face-seen? if
		0.22 pen!
		[ 28 0 -6 ] [ 25 0 -6 ] [ 25 2.3 -6 ] [ 28 2.3 -6 ] 11 hatch
	then ;

\ fruit trees scattered over a stretch of ground, each seeded from its place
: orchard-trees ( west east south north count seed -- )
	| west east south north count seed |
	[ 0 count 1 do k
		seed k 5.1 * + hash-fraction east west - * west + to x
		seed k 8.3 * + 1.1 + hash-fraction north south - * south + to z
		[ x z seed k + ]
	loop ] to trees
	[ view@x view@z ] to eye
	trees ( tree | tree first eye first - sq tree second eye second - sq + negate ) sort-by
	( tree | tree spread to tree-seed to z to x x z 4.2 tree-seed hash-fraction 1.2 * + tree-seed fruit-tree ) each ;

\ rows of rose bushes across a bed, the farthest drawn first
: rose-rows ( west east south north n-rows n-across seed -- )
	| west east south north n-rows n-across seed |
	[ view@x view@z ] to eye
	[ 0 n-rows 1 do row
		0 n-across 1 do across
			east west - across 0.5 + row 2 mod 0.4 * + n-across / * west + to x
			north south - row 0.5 + n-rows / * south + to z
			[ x z seed row 31 * + across + ]
		loop
	loop ] ( bush | bush first eye first - sq bush second eye second - sq + negate ) sort-by
	( bush | bush spread rose-bush ) each ;

\ the ladder where the plot has put it: leaning against a balcony, lying on the ground, or not here at all
: ladder-for ( room lean-foot lean-top ground-a ground-b leaning -- )
	| room lean-foot lean-top ground-a ground-b leaning |
	:ladder room inside? not if exit then
	leaning if lean-foot lean-top leaning-ladder exit then
	ground-a ground-b lying-ladder ;

\ === Front Path ===

\ the front door and step seen from the path
: front-path-picture ( -- )
	0.9 1.65 -10.5 -0.05 0.1 270 outdoor-view
	[ [ [ -2.1 0 -4.2 ] PI 0.2 + ] [ [ 2.5 0 -3.8 ] PI 0.25 - ] [ [ -4.3 0 -6.4 ] PI 0.35 + ] ] spots!
	0.06 pen!
	-12 12 -7 -0.6 10 5 lawn-rows
	0.14 pen!
	-8 8 -7 -0.7 90 43 grass-strokes
	robner-house
	:newspaper :front-path inside? if newspaper-at-door then
	0.4 pen!
	-0.9 0 -7 -0.9 0 -0.6 edge
	0.9 0 -7 0.9 0 -0.6 edge
	0.55 pen!
	0 70 1 do k
		k 0.43 * hash-fraction 1.6 * 0.8 - to across
		k 0.71 * hash-fraction 6 * -6.8 + to along
		across 0.005 along across 0.025 + 0.005 along 0.015 + edge
	loop
	:front-path [ 0 0 0 ] [ 0 0 0 ] [ -3.5 0.05 -5.5 ] [ -2.6 0.05 -1.9 ] false ladder-for
	outdoor-done ;

